; The Lathe-written linker (lathe/src/link.lth) on the BBC Model B+128, at the full capacities, the
; ones that link the compiler and the linker itself (LKSMALL 0: lathe/src/lk_tab.lth). This is the
; developer's form, `*RUN LLINK ARGS`, its banks in the module's RAM form (slot 4), loaded by the
; start-up code; bbcrom.rom_env makes the ROM form's environment from it (its banks numbered after
; the compiler's, 6 to 10, read only, the window $8050-$BFDF), started by `*LLINK ARGS` or `*LLINK
; @FILE` from the image that holds the compiler too (lathe/tests/test_bbc_toolchain.py;
; lathe/docs/bbc.md, "Step 5, as built" and "The linker links the compiler").
;
; Fixed in main RAM: what every phase calls many times, lk_tab, lk_rec, lk_sym, sys, bbc and the
; run-time (rt_bbc, rt_math), as on Wendy 2 (linker-bank.env); the functions with `with` blocks,
; which the linker keeps fixed (lk_name's accessors of `local`, those of the work area's node
; columns); and the tables not in a region: the functions' columns but fn_edge, the variables'
; and constants', the classes', lk_envf.text, the command file's words. A bank of the module is
; 16 KB where Wendy 2's are 28: lk_graph and lk_alloc, which share a bank there, are 17.6 KB as
; the linker judges them, so the code takes five banks. Bank 1: link, lk_err (its messages too),
; lk_file, lk_envf. Bank 2, the reading: lk_scan and lk_name. Bank 3: lk_graph, lk_win and
; lk_boot. Bank 4: lk_alloc. Bank 5, placement and output: lk_place, lk_fix, lk_map, lk_emit,
; lk_out and lk_op.
;
; Regions, in three sideways RAM slots (the slots are free while the linker runs: the compiler's
; tables are there only while *LATHE runs, and its constants in slot 13 are copied again at each
; *LATHE), read only through functions with blocks, kept fixed (lk_tab.wk and set_wk, the
; accessors of lk_tab and lk_name, and the readers of the hottest work columns in lk_graph,
; lk_alloc and lk_fix): slot 0, lk_name.local (8,000 bytes) and the slots' columns (8,256);
; slot 1, the calls (8,992) and the work area's node columns (3,600); slot 12, the rest of the
; work area (14,400). Slot 13 is not used.
;
; The split (2026-11-16): one, $4000, for both forms and both BBCFS settings. bbcfs is fixed in
; the developer's form, whose start-up loads the banks through bbc.open, which with BBCFS 1 calls
; bbcfs.map (a bank is not there before it is loaded), and in bank 1 in the ROM form, whose banks
; are always there: the `when ROMFORM` entry is the ROM form's alone, since bbcrom.rom_env
; defines ROMFORM as 1 (lathe/docs/configurations.md, "The environment file").
;
; With `define ADFS 1` main RAM starts at $1F00, ADFS's PAGE with the DFS beside it (BBCFS 2,
; ADFS's names): the `when ADFS` entries, with the split at $4600 for both forms (measured
; 2026-11-17: the code ended at $44BD in the developer's form and $427A in the ROM form;
; lathe/docs/bbc.md, "ADFS").
;
; The 128 KB module (eight banks: lathe/docs/bbc.md, "The 128 KB module"): bbcrom.rom_env with
; eight banks defines ROM128 as 1, and the `when ROM128` and `unless ROM128` entries put the
; linker in three banks, the image's 5 to 7, chosen by the far calls between modules
; (lathe/tests/farcall_matrix.py): bank 1 link, lk_err, lk_file, lk_envf, lk_win, lk_place,
; lk_fix, lk_emit and lk_boot (its callers, lk_emit and lk_place, are there, and what it calls);
; bank 2 lk_scan, lk_name and lk_map; bank 3 lk_graph and lk_alloc (whose calls between them were
; 1,150,365 of the 1,276,580 far calls of the compiler's link in five banks); lk_out and lk_op
; fixed. As the linker judges them they are 15,309, 15,079 and 16,031 bytes of 16,272 on
; 2026-11-17, in the ROM form, whose lk_err holds no texts (TEXTS_IN_MODULE, below; the ADFS build's
; bank 1 with bbcfs 15,934): lathe/tests/test_bbc_rom128.py is the gate.
;
; The texts of the errors: in the developer's form in lk_err; in the ROM form written by the
; module image (`when ROMFORM define TEXTS_IN_MODULE 1`; lathe/docs/bbc.md, "The texts in the
; module").
;
; A 32K BBC Model B (`define RAM32 1`; lathe/docs/bbc.md, "The linker on a 32K BBC"): no
; sideways RAM, so no `bank` entry for a slot and no `region` entry, and the regions are in main
; RAM with the rest, which is $1900-$7BFF and $0401-$06FF as on the B+128 in mode 7; the module is
; the eight-bank ROM, as above. The capacities are the 32K build's (`LKSMALL 2`: lathe/src/
; lk_tab.lth), which fill main RAM beside the resident part.
cpu       6502
zeropage  $00 $8F
define    ROMFORM 0     ; the developer's form; bbcrom.rom_env makes it 1, the ROM form
define    ADFS 0        ; 1: PAGE is ADFS's with the DFS beside it, $1F00 (lathe/docs/bbc.md, "ADFS")
define    RAM32 0       ; 1: a 32K Model B, every table in main RAM (lathe/docs/bbc.md, "The linker on a 32K BBC")
define    ADAPT 0       ; 1: the image for every machine with sideways RAM (below; the ROM form, ADFS 1)
unless    RAM32 unless ADFS code $1900 $3FFF
unless    RAM32 unless ADFS data $4000 $7BFF
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT when ADFS code $1F00 $45FF
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT when ADFS data $4600 $7BFF
when      ADAPT code $1F00 $47DF  ; the image for every machine with sideways RAM: its list (below)
when      ADAPT data $47E0 $7BFF  ; after the code, which is free once rt_place has read it
when      RAM32 code $1900 $3A12
when      RAM32 data $3A13 $7BFF
more      data $0401 $06FF
exit      return $0400  ; the start-up code keeps S at $0400 (bbc.KEEP), and ends with RTS
output    raw
define    BOARD 3       ; the BBC (lathe/host/driver/boards.py)
define    PORTS 2       ; lathe/src/sys.lth over lathe/rt/bbc.lth
define    BBCFS 0       ; file names as given; 1 the DFS's, 2 ADFS's, 3 those of the one OSARGS names (lathe/rt/bbc/bbcfs.lth)
unless    ROMFORM define TEXTS_IN_MODULE 0  ; the texts of the errors in the tool
when      ROMFORM define TEXTS_IN_MODULE 1  ; the ROM form's, in the module (lathe/docs/bbc.md, "The texts in the module")
define    MODULE_SLOT 4 ; the module's slot: rt_bbc.SLOT, and the emulator's --bbc-module-slot
unless    RAM32 define LKSMALL 0 ; the linker's tables at full size (lathe/src/lk_tab.lth)
when      RAM32 define LKSMALL 2   ; the 32K build's
unless    ROMFORM define LKDYN 1  ; dynamic regions linked (lathe/src/lk_dyn.lth); not in the ROM
when      ROMFORM define LKDYN 0    ; forms, for the room of the 128 KB image (lathe/docs/bbc.md)
define    ROM128 0      ; five banks; bbcrom.rom_env makes it 1 for the eight-bank image: three
window    WIN $8000 $BFDF
switch    WIN bank farcall
bank      WIN 1 $81 LLINK1.BIN
bank      WIN 2 $82 LLINK2.BIN
bank      WIN 3 $83 LLINK3.BIN
unless    ROM128 bank WIN 4 $84 LLINK4.BIN
unless    ROM128 bank WIN 5 $85 LLINK5.BIN
unless    RAM32 bank WIN 20 $00 ; sideways slot 0: lk_name.local, the slots' columns
unless    RAM32 bank WIN 21 $01 ; sideways slot 1: the calls, the work area's node columns
unless    RAM32 bank WIN 22 $0C ; sideways slot 12: the work area
unless    ADFS place link WIN 1
when      ADFS unless ROM128 place link WIN 1
when      ADFS when ROM128 place link WIN 2   ; called once: room in bank 1 for ADFS's bbcfs (bbc.md, "Link error 62")
place     lk_err WIN 1
place     lk_file WIN 1
place     lk_envf WIN 1
when      ROMFORM place bbcfs WIN 1 ; bbc.lth's file names with BBCFS 1; fixed in the developer's form
place     lk_scan WIN 2
place     lk_name WIN 2
place     lk_graph WIN 3
unless    ROM128 place lk_win WIN 3
unless    ROM128 place lk_boot WIN 3
unless    ROM128 place lk_alloc WIN 4
unless    ROM128 place lk_op WIN 5
unless    ROM128 place lk_fix WIN 5
unless    ROM128 place lk_place WIN 5
unless    ROM128 place lk_map WIN 5
unless    ROM128 place lk_emit WIN 5
unless    ROM128 place lk_out WIN 5
unless    ROM128 place lk_dyn WIN 5   ; the list of a dynamic region's places (lk_emit calls it)
when      ROM128 place lk_win WIN 1
when      ROM128 place lk_place WIN 1
when      ROM128 place lk_fix WIN 1
when      ROM128 place lk_emit WIN 1
when      ROM128 place lk_boot WIN 1
when      ROM128 place lk_map WIN 2
when      ROM128 place lk_dyn WIN 2   ; the list of a dynamic region's places: the bank with room
when      ROM128 place lk_alloc WIN 3
when      RAM32 when ROM128 place lk_out WIN 2  ; the 32K build: in the bank with room, out of main RAM
when      RAM32 when ROM128 place lk_op WIN 2
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region LKLOCAL WIN 20   ; lk_name.local
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region LKCALLS WIN 21   ; lk_tab.edge_word and fn_edge
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region LKSLOTS WIN 20   ; lk_tab.slot_sz, slot_weight, big_slot and big_size
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region LKNODES WIN 21   ; lk_tab.nodes: the work area's node columns
unless    RAM32 unless ADAPT region LKWORK WIN 22    ; lk_tab.work: the rest of the work area
; The image for every machine with sideways RAM (ADAPT 1, with ADFS 1: lathe/docs/bbc.md, "One
; image for every machine with sideways RAM"): the same regions, each `dynamic`, which rt_place
; puts in main RAM as it starts where they fit, in the order of these entries, the work area's
; node columns first (entered most for their bytes); what does not fit stays in its slot.
when      ADAPT region LKNODES WIN 21 dynamic
when      ADAPT region LKSLOTS WIN 20 dynamic
when      ADAPT region LKLOCAL WIN 20 dynamic
when      ADAPT region LKCALLS WIN 21 dynamic
when      ADAPT region LKWORK WIN 22 dynamic
when      ADAPT placer rt_place
; The 32K build's regions are in main RAM, and the compiler is told so (-fNAME, FIXED_REGIONS:
; lathe/host/README.md, "The environment file"), so that a function with a block of one of them
; is not kept in fixed memory, but for LKWORK: lk_alloc's and lk_graph's readers of the work area
; moved into their bank would put it 55 bytes over as judged in the eight-bank form (ROM128), so
; there their blocks still map (slot 0, which is harmless: what runs inside is fixed); in the
; sixteen-bank form, which the 32K image is (lathe/docs/bbc.md, "The 32K Model B"), LKWORK too.
when      RAM32 define FIXED_REGIONS 1
when      RAM32 region LKLOCAL fixed
when      RAM32 region LKCALLS fixed
when      RAM32 region LKSLOTS fixed
when      RAM32 region LKNODES fixed
when      RAM32 unless ROM128 region LKWORK fixed
farcall   rt_bbc
